@startuml
title RuleSphere - Communication Diagram\n06. REST / gRPC Evaluation | UC-21..24
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam objectBackgroundColor #E9F8ED
skinparam objectBorderColor #496477
skinparam ArrowColor #496477
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 60
object "client : ConsumerApplication" as Client <<actor>>
object "api : REST/gRPC Adapter" as API <<boundary>>
object "auth : AuthorizationService" as Auth <<service>>
object "evaluation : EvaluationService" as Service <<coordinator>>
object "resolver : SnapshotResolver" as Resolver <<service>>
object "store : LocalArtifactStore" as Store <<entity>>
object "schema : SchemaVersion" as Schema <<entity>>
object "executor : GraphExecutor" as Executor <<service>>
object "node : DecisionNode" as Node <<entity>>
object "capture : TraceCaptureService" as Trace <<service>>
Client --> API : 1: evaluate(input, credential, context, optional pin)
API --> Auth : 1.1: authorize credential and Tenant/Workspace scope
API --> Service : 1.2 [authorized]: evaluate(request)
Service --> Resolver : 1.2.1: resolveEligible(request)
Resolver --> Store : 1.2.1.1a [pinned]: get exact eligible version\n1.2.1.1b [unpinned]: get local Active / selected Canary
Resolver --> Resolver : 1.2.1.2 [available]: bind atomic snapshot
Service --> Schema : 1.2.2 [snapshot resolved]: validate input
Service --> Executor : 1.2.3 [valid input]: execute(snapshot, input)
Executor --> Node : 1.2.3.1 *[activated and execution healthy]: evaluate(context)
Executor --> Executor : 1.2.3.2 *: record result / typed fallback / fail-fast
Service --> Trace : 1.2.4 [auditable execution] <<async>>: capture result/error and tree
API ..> Client : 1.3: result + executionId OR explicit error
note bottom of Resolver
Pin unavailable/ineligible => REST 412 or gRPC equivalent.
No silent fallback to Active; stop this evaluation path.
Unpinned unavailable => protocol-defined availability error.
Canary routing is deterministic for fixed configuration.
end note
note bottom of Executor
Loop 1.2.3.1-1.2.3.2 follows topological order.
Skip inactive branches. Qualifying error + valid typed fallback:
record fallback and continue; otherwise fail-fast.
Input errors stop before graph execution.
end note
note bottom of Service
No synchronous Control Plane dependency.
One fixed graph/schema/dependency snapshot for the whole execution.
Publication during execution cannot replace its snapshot.
end note
legend bottom
  Nested numbers identify calls; a/b are mutually exclusive alternatives.
  * denotes repetition; [condition] is a guard; <<async>> is an asynchronous send.
  Routine returns omitted; ..> is the displayed response; errors stop dependent calls.
endlegend
@enduml
